{
  "$comment": "#EXP-1616 (eCode E3, #NEW-36) THE REPO PAGE ×4 + the Settings › Repositories additions; genUI catalogue components only, mockups approved. SETTINGS › REPOSITORIES (settings-repositories ×4): every row carries a `Badge` naming its provider (`copy.provider.github` | `copy.provider.ecode`) and, when `repoChecksRollup` over its PRs is non-null, a `Chip{dot}` with that state (success | pending | failure). Tapping a row opens its repo page. `Add repository` (owners) opens a `Dialog` (web, desktop) or a `Drawer` (phones): `ChoiceTiles` (`copy.add.github` | `copy.add.ecode`); for Exponential an `Input` (`copy.add.name`, a name of [A-Za-z0-9._-]), a `Select` (`copy.add.defaultBranch`, `main` default, `master`, `develop`), a `SettingsRow` + `Switch` (`copy.add.mirror`, revealing an `Input` for the mirror URL) and `FormActions` (`copy.add.cancel` / `copy.add.create`); GitHub keeps the existing connect flow. THE REPO PAGE (view `repo`, route `/t/$teamSlug/repos/$name?tab=`, `repoTab(tab)` picks the tab, unknown = pulls): `Page` + `AppBar` (the repo's name, its provider `Badge`) + `Tabs{pill}` over `tabs` in order. PULL REQUESTS = `Section{tree:true}` of `repoPrTree(prs)` rows: `Row{depth, identifier, title, subtitle, meta}`; meta = the `Chip{dot}` of `checks` (none when null) then the merge-train `Badge` (merge-train.json `statusPill`, from the row's merge fields); a draft row reads the draft pill. Only live PRs (open | draft). A PR's parent = the live PR whose head is its base (lowest number when two share a head); roots newest first, children oldest first, depth-first; a loop of live PRs (no root) starts at its newest member, depth 0, the others nested under it. BRANCHES = `Section` of `repoBranches` rows: `Row{title: name, subtitle: sha, meta}` with a `Badge` `copy.branches.default` on the default branch and the PR identifier `#n` of a live PR on it; the default first, then code-point order. RUNS = an `EmptyState` (`copy.runs.empty`) until eCode CI (#EXP-1617, E4) fills the tab; the tab and its route stay. SETTINGS = `SettingsRow`s: provider (`Badge`), default branch (`Select` over the branches, owners), the clone URL (`exp://<team>/<name>`, copyable), backups (`Row` per backup, newest first, + `copy.settings.restore` → `AlertDialog` `copy.settings.restoreTitle` / `copy.settings.restoreConfirm`, owners), mirror (`Switch` + `Input`, owners). Desktop also lists the PR tree in the IDE sidebar with the same Section/Row tree. FEEDBACK (feedback-states.json): skeleton rows on first load, an empty tab = its `EmptyState` (`copy.pulls.empty`, `copy.branches.empty`), a failed action = a toast. Replayed by packages/domain-contract (bun test), desktop domain::repo_page, iOS ExpCore RepoPage, Android domain RepoPage: every mirror replays `treeCases`, `branchCases`, `rollupCases` and `tabCases`, comparing the WHOLE result.",
